//
// Expected: c0a0e1 at two sessions, c0a0e0 at one. Read the one-session
// verdict for the argument this model was written to make; the two-session
// divergence is a separate and later finding, described after it.
//
// An anonymous Diffie-Hellman exchange with both public
// keys sent UNGUARDED, which is normally the definition of a man in the
// middle, made safe by a pre-shared key used for nothing but confirming the
// transcript. Every value the attacker might substitute is covered by a MAC it
// cannot produce, so every substitution halts the recipient instead of
// steering it.
//
// At two sessions the equivalence query fails, and the reason is worth the
// space. The confirmation MAC covers `gb` and nothing else, so replaying a
// sibling session's (gb, conf_b) pair whole gets past Alice's ASSERT on its
// own merits: the MAC is Bob's, just from the wrong run. Alice then derives
// DH_KEX(gb#2, a) while Bob still holds DH_KEX(ga, b), and the two disagree.
// Confirming the transcript is not the same as confirming which run produced
// it, and nothing here binds the exchange to one. Substitution is still
// impossible, which is why both other queries hold at either session count.
//
// The one-session verdict is the point: this is the shape the unguarded MitM
// models in this directory are missing, and it says that guards in a Verifpal
// model stand in for an authentication mechanism rather than for magic. The
// equivalence query is the strongest of the three — not merely "the attacker
// learns nothing" but "the two of them agree", which is what key confirmation
// is actually for.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private psk
	generates a
	ga = PUBKEY(a)
	conf_a = MAC(psk, ga)
]

Alice -> Bob: ga, conf_a

principal Bob[
	knows private psk
	generates b
	gb = PUBKEY(b)
	_ = ASSERT(MAC(psk, ga), conf_a)?
	conf_b = MAC(psk, gb)
	k_bob = DH_KEX(ga, b)
]

Bob -> Alice: gb, conf_b

principal Alice[
	knows private m
	_ = ASSERT(MAC(psk, gb), conf_b)?
	k_alice = DH_KEX(gb, a)
	sealed = AEAD_ENC(k_alice, m, nil)
]

Alice -> Bob: sealed

principal Bob[
	opened = AEAD_DEC(k_bob, sealed, nil)?
	_ = HASH(opened)
]

queries[
	confidentiality? m
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: ga
	equivalence? k_alice, k_bob
]
